\ echo.fam — its arguments, spaced, then a newline; with -n first, no
\ newline (a long line written in pieces: the console takes lines of 63
\ bytes at most).
: enl variable ;
-1 lit enl !  1 lit
dup arg ?dup if "-n" streq if 0 lit enl !  1 lit + then then
dup begin dup arg ?dup while over 3 lit pick u> if 20 lit putc then puts 1 lit + repeat 2drop
enl @ if 0A lit putc then bye
